#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119537 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/id #uuid "9552ad30-9d46-5884-9877-18ca8842c252" :question/math-academy-id "e-4775" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b},$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/45cefb7311cd5253b76164cc7f2f3ce01b445f0e9061b720865227128b60debe.png)\nIf $\\langle x_1,x_2 \\rangle$ and $\\langle y_1,y_2 \\rangle$ are the solutions to the systems $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ and $L\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{b}$ respectively, what is the value of $x_1 \\cdot y_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/b521c0b31d05de273d0abd37e00b046c0e36ed47ef30d22784a24cace4d676f9.png)\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/9dcc9f71745cce72ce7e122b3bc8cd7064d05f3be90d712202f42956956ef18e.png)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=6 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=6$ and $y_2=4.$ Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/903fbfe6828526dace264d65baebf58c31e36db8a54e25ed1f3be859e6079ebb.png)\n\n- Next, we solve $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/dcb234ae13cab2676ea5afa7fde452c870ff5088ff5748342c517bf2a96327a8.png)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $x_2=-2$ and $x_1=2.$ Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/53bace542ba4dfd0d7e5e4bf9b6451c7f39502dd1bf24d030f654050629f0e0d.png)\n\nFinally, $x_1 \\cdot y_2 = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119538 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "24bc4954-462b-5066-83d4-8a4a87efc7b7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4777" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/f88cbbb9459dd3b467e6b87d230ad23634461597aa9d8da3e933774273e2ab2f.png)\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/7704f9285f14f496bb9f1721d188866c9464c585e33235c5cc6eee42e3f3a3eb.png)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/712643d674cf8a7a086a9a935659d86bba7bd2fb25f131ec56e798cfc1d538d9.png)\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4 \\\\ {y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =4-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =4-(2) \\\\  & =2, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1-(2)+2(2) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/151dc664a131df0f3e13f2997bb1af6d41586b5f4dcf8a1acd1342f85e1b9c92.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119630 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cbefba9a-eda2-5a8e-8bb5-59ea4175b835" :question/math-academy-id "e-8926" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/fd1cf7c3d929fb79576a59d4ef3aebd3f24a0d570c938ab80ebd44c5bd4c238f.png)\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/b521c0b31d05de273d0abd37e00b046c0e36ed47ef30d22784a24cace4d676f9.png)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 66\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ 15{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=5$ and $y_2=-9.$ \n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/ccb4ab47d3a270cf9545d4f79e6f90b944cf6121fca3752eeee6ddc712fcfdec.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56c5bcfe-6205-516a-8e5c-62e6bb91a262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344306} {:answer/id #uuid "a80cd910-3693-5f5c-8ef9-61565e976cc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344307} {:answer/id #uuid "686b9bde-5fc4-5081-8505-1444454999b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344308} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b7909f-1434-5259-bfd8-8ab317acca69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344309} {:answer/id #uuid "174bc5c5-2fdc-584d-a846-2c0dffae8daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "174bc5c5-2fdc-584d-a846-2c0dffae8daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344310} :answer-field/id #uuid "6179c6a6-401d-5aaf-a06a-dfeb3a7510c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b452cf4-4d72-5df1-88c6-867fd46459f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-104861" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions of the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of the product ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=1 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=1$ and ${y}_{2}=4.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 4=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "566bdfde-c0a4-5796-be5e-7cd5e50579a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344313} {:answer/id #uuid "8b4c3882-1627-5504-b957-3c822235e005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344314} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d352e2-8e04-5228-b869-1a250961968f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344315} {:answer/id #uuid "1e67d3f3-3a90-5dd5-837e-6ca206c4c9ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344316} {:answer/id #uuid "3e4ddcc9-2dd0-5b3e-a2ed-a03e03591bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e67d3f3-3a90-5dd5-837e-6ca206c4c9ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344316} :answer-field/id #uuid "394f08d2-a60d-54f1-855a-a182a6b80b59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc9812ca-2c1e-56fa-b8ed-8a5c02f7892a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105755" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=2$ and ${y}_{2}=-9.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d992b61-49b4-581f-9299-c049b5ce54e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344320} {:answer/id #uuid "c965cddd-b8d0-5acb-9540-025df157f1c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344321} {:answer/id #uuid "9567ad29-733c-5c2f-a159-0d650178ed9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344322} {:answer/id #uuid "69b5bd77-d816-58d0-818f-309d6afbf5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344323} {:answer/id #uuid "85ec0a08-c2ff-5f17-b85a-64e04f84da22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c965cddd-b8d0-5acb-9540-025df157f1c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344321} :answer-field/id #uuid "068455de-b3c7-58b7-9eb3-0cd600079a56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6903c088-f681-52de-b192-228090b5bbcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-105760" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=7 \\\\ -10{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=7$ and ${y}_{2}=34.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21728b58-90de-55ba-8000-436d971398ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344327} {:answer/id #uuid "690bf126-090b-5102-95bc-f4a80871a60b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344328} {:answer/id #uuid "83fb84e2-a967-55c8-86c5-35f26ee6c4d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344329} {:answer/id #uuid "80ef11ca-5748-5584-a45c-0e0691130d73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344330} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3d90d0-d170-5fd5-b024-7aac8f373a22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21728b58-90de-55ba-8000-436d971398ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344327} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f3f89bc-6f02-532d-960c-28af7784a2ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ba1dd2a-ca92-52b3-9b03-af5073d0982e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105928" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-7 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=3 \\\\ 3{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-7, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =3+{y}_{1} \\\\  & =3+(-7) \\\\  & =-4, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =3-3{y}_{2} \\\\  & =3-3(-4) \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84a7c668-c6d9-5e60-8898-a2aa67042427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344334} {:answer/id #uuid "32ad1aa6-86b1-5ef7-b68d-ff7b983268cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344335} {:answer/id #uuid "f702670b-f819-5e07-af5e-9b311b04e5e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344336} {:answer/id #uuid "c120872c-2781-5058-80be-f0dec35cef87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344337} {:answer/id #uuid "d709fdcf-0cee-5ac2-a34a-8c0e487f30c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d709fdcf-0cee-5ac2-a34a-8c0e487f30c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344338} :answer-field/id #uuid "23fd2f2e-4c2c-5598-b03f-bcf5f10743e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b49c135b-ee7c-514c-acd4-fa5185ae6537" :question/math-academy-id "q-105930" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-2 \\\\ 9{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2-9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2-9(-2) \\\\  & =16, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1+4{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1+4(-2)-(16) \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7f0b926-5f55-5455-9a5b-f2214b4ab48f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -70 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344341} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1f34c6-2812-509c-8066-a24b14f002c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 70 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344342} {:answer/id #uuid "07d108f8-d626-582c-8c9a-e882553f00db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344343} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8f2d82-5fdb-5363-a67e-a93400ee221f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -63 \\\\ 81\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344344} {:answer/id #uuid "c5625959-4513-57a3-a02b-bce0f878c626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 56 \\\\ -80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07d108f8-d626-582c-8c9a-e882553f00db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344343} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f6146d-2a6a-5ef3-88d9-37de88387dff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2491212f-7897-5f32-9dfc-f8262f2e00da" :question/math-academy-id "q-105934" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=9 \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=7 \\\\ -9{y}_{1}+{y}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =9, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =7-7{y}_{1} \\\\  & =7-7(9) \\\\  & =-56, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-1+9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1+9(9) \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8e8eeb2-e460-525b-b83b-0cefde5b0d62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116596} {:answer/id #uuid "e5632857-fcc6-5529-9013-36dcdc488696" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116597} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b956a9-3e83-59e1-a072-df57460b7c1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116598} {:answer/id #uuid "37018c59-4769-58b3-8e67-fc888628b07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116599} {:answer/id #uuid "47d1a930-1a53-5630-a9ae-8ba4ca728ca5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6b956a9-3e83-59e1-a072-df57460b7c1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116598} :answer-field/id #uuid "9daf47c2-7d9f-58bf-8651-26039aeaed59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cc6bf17a-cfc4-5f52-984e-78af80897af9" :question/math-academy-id "q-105949" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-1 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-1$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=2$ and ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}=(-1)\\cdot (-1)=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6de57ac-1896-5292-9c6e-d8ffa638a6aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344348} {:answer/id #uuid "59a3963c-d2c4-592c-ad81-30318af760f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344349} {:answer/id #uuid "4460d39c-46ba-5545-8a3d-56dd2b9297cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344350} {:answer/id #uuid "14ae2984-b59e-5742-9b76-668a651d69f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344351} {:answer/id #uuid "26f8e74c-f5d6-5098-a661-a511e07688ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14ae2984-b59e-5742-9b76-668a651d69f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344351} :answer-field/id #uuid "e859a6a4-14d8-5c00-9c52-e8623c14f4cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1861ef9a-574a-56cc-89ee-9ea58e347255" :question/math-academy-id "q-105951" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=6 \\\\ 4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=6$ and ${y}_{2}=-4.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{2}=(-1)\\cdot (-4)=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3028f5d5-fe41-5fee-81df-8ca8c4490ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{130}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344355} {:answer/id #uuid "a96fe158-7918-5827-a6bc-7956b8cafcf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356} {:answer/id #uuid "a1651cfe-7f95-52c3-a899-4b2098c85460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344357} {:answer/id #uuid "9f929d96-7b48-5baa-9dfc-6c07b4b71fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344358} {:answer/id #uuid "dcb46c83-6082-52d5-9863-c7dc89f7326a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a96fe158-7918-5827-a6bc-7956b8cafcf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecdc2461-243e-5a09-bec5-42d4b5e7879e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af800076-1dc9-5a0d-bd5f-a7e1f437d795" :question/math-academy-id "q-105953" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=14.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-7$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{26}{7}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{26}{7} \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=\\frac{26}{7}\\cdot 14=52.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorizati