lution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ -7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=33.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 33\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271469cd-1d30-58f7-a825-dbb12578bf77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344369} {:answer/id #uuid "bf71b510-4ac3-53b8-9901-250c61e149ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344370} {:answer/id #uuid "2fadf827-734c-5872-88c6-3ad921566526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344371} {:answer/id #uuid "e5d2debb-25e3-52f3-ae2e-069d9ea65c8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344372} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ad9ba9-425a-563b-af47-47532c73c582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fadf827-734c-5872-88c6-3ad921566526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344371} :answer-field/id #uuid "f983b39e-12e6-5c41-a0db-99e5bfff64cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed3602c3-c2aa-5ab4-82c9-5f20305df86b" :question/math-academy-id "q-107172" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=0 \\\\ -6{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=0$ and ${y}_{2}=4.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b60c563-fb5a-54a2-86d1-f756e053812d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344376} {:answer/id #uuid "8d17ad9a-cf6f-51c8-b1fb-4c9701d0008f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344377} {:answer/id #uuid "3e36c1e3-a73a-5e07-9d4f-e4c13d37dde2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344378} {:answer/id #uuid "02a8026f-f875-583b-aa85-4393cddae5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344379} {:answer/id #uuid "07fd990b-e915-5cb9-ba9d-886fd2b34251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e36c1e3-a73a-5e07-9d4f-e4c13d37dde2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344378} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b1f1f45-b7d9-551d-827f-85ef8a97e75b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "910827ac-326a-5bf3-8b02-67a9b84939ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-107174" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-2 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-1-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1-(-2) \\\\  & =1, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-3+4{y}_{2}+{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-3+4(1)+(-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0f2072f-768a-56b1-9616-0b7e0993f827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344383} {:answer/id #uuid "271bcefe-4deb-51ab-9494-33415f491eaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344384} {:answer/id #uuid "2df462be-e488-5d12-b16f-f25d8b8f6061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344385} {:answer/id #uuid "3b09b760-8f1b-5fb2-a968-da0775ffefa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344386} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f3d211-3327-5a09-b4db-423cd5065931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8f3d211-3327-5a09-b4db-423cd5065931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344387} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab533481-7486-5f37-8712-eebe8309d795" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8eaf079f-b6a4-5f80-b8a8-2783953d0262" :question/math-academy-id "q-32570" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-4$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-4+3(-\\frac{2}{3})=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344388 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0253d206-7026-516e-98b2-02200d06f35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344390} {:answer/id #uuid "3de600f1-f8f9-55e2-9d8f-959b26fbf2e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344391} {:answer/id #uuid "066d2459-3b81-5c26-ae95-31663c40e7a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344392} {:answer/id #uuid "1b9ca9be-29ea-538a-8c3c-7dbd606ad9d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344393} {:answer/id #uuid "f94a053c-a4c7-55d0-ae6e-49526e2fa75e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3de600f1-f8f9-55e2-9d8f-959b26fbf2e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344391} :answer-field/id #uuid "2673fb90-0289-5806-a7d7-4997a8d37c8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "338b1c4a-b1f5-53a7-9d9d-a5d1100b37c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-32647" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=2$ and ${y}_{2}=6.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d005d91-5f07-5a77-89b8-76000a116fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344397} {:answer/id #uuid "d6772212-08df-57a4-aa46-faccc338fc74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344398} {:answer/id #uuid "a638ac67-b4b7-5351-a3e8-120d6ad12482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344399} {:answer/id #uuid "b71b43e6-cf84-58b3-85be-05cfbaaa087c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344400} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a59a72-0496-52b9-841f-b8710c7cc3bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0a59a72-0496-52b9-841f-b8710c7cc3bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344401} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b7728b0-6a69-57b1-a89d-e6e4f0d7ee54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c3924e4-a03d-5fb7-a5cd-f6c273cb45fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-32671" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=3 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =3, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-1+4{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1+4(3) \\\\  & =11, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =4-3{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =4-3(3)-2(11) \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
